{"name":"Zǎo Hóng Maroon","hex":"#c1264c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maroon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An escaped black slave of the Caribbean and the Americas or a descendant of such a person. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A castaway; a person who has been marooned (abandoned)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Associated with Maroon culture, communities or peoples."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maroon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jujube","blocks":[{"text":"Jujube, jujuba, Chinese jujube, red date or Chinese date is a species in the genus Ziziphus in the buckthorn family Rhamnaceae. It is often confused with the closely related Indian jujube, Z. mauritiana. The jujube tolerates a diverse range of climates, from temperate to tropical. Its origin is thought to be in eastern Asia, but it has been widely dispersed through cultivation, and is today cultivated in gardens as a shrub as well as in agriculture as a food crop. Its fruit is eaten freshly harvested as well as dried and candied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Ziziphus_jujuba.jpg/330px-Ziziphus_jujuba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jujube","wikidata":"Q11181633"},{"title":"Maroon","blocks":[{"text":"Maroon is a brownish red color that takes its name from the French word marron, meaning chestnut. Marron is also one of the French translations for \"brown\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg/330px-Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maroon","wikidata":"Q25393814"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Azufaifas_%28fcm%29.jpg/500px-Azufaifas_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content